{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"769","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Cycle In Maze"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"15 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Robot is in a rectangular maze of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each cell of the maze is either empty or occupied by an obstacle. The Robot can move between neighboring cells on the side left (the symbol \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"), right (the symbol \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"), up (the symbol \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\") or down (the symbol \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"). The Robot can move to the cell only if it is empty. Initially, the Robot is in the empty cell."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to find "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lexicographically minimal"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" Robot's cycle with length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":", which begins and ends in the cell where the Robot was initially. It is allowed to the Robot to visit any cell many times (including starting)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider that Robot's way is given as a line which consists of symbols \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". For example, if firstly the Robot goes down, then left, then right and up, it means that his way is written as \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"DLRU"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this task you "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"don't need"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to minimize the length of the way. Find the minimum lexicographical (in alphabet order as in the dictionary) line which satisfies requirements above."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, m ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ k ≤ 106"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the size of the maze and the length of the cycle. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the following "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" symbols — the description of the maze. If the symbol equals to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" the current cell is empty. If the symbol equals to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"*"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" the current cell is occupied by an obstacle. If the symbol equals to \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" then initially the Robot is in this cell and it is empty. It is guaranteed that the symbol \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is found in the maze exactly once. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the lexicographically minimum Robot's way with the length exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":", which starts and ends in the cell where initially Robot is. If there is no such way, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"IMPOSSIBLE"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"(without quotes)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 3 2\n.**\nX..\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"RL\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 6 14\n..***.\n*...X.\n..*...\n..*.**\n....*.\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"DLDDLLLRRRUURU\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 3 4\n***\n*X*\n***\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"IMPOSSIBLE\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample two cyclic ways for the Robot with the length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" exist — \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"UD"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RL"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". The second cycle is lexicographically less. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample the Robot should move in the following way: down, left, down, down, left, left, left, right, right, right, up, up, right, up. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sample the Robot can't move to the neighboring cells, because they are occupied by obstacles."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"769C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/769/problem/C"}